      "side": 1,
      "message": "Some APIs may have restrictions even though they\u0027re stubbed and stable, so the safeness here depends on there being source builds in development branches to catch inadvertent use. That seems likely, but is it safe to assume it\u0027s always the case?\n\nA way to tighten this up a bit more is to make Soong check visibility on the corresponding source modules, even when the prebuilts are in use. The remaining gap would then be builds that only have the prebuilts and not the sources, which are much more uncommon (master-art is one, and fwiw the only one I\u0027m aware of).\n\nI don\u0027t have a strong opinion on if it\u0027s worth the extra complexity, though.\n\n(If that approach is chosen then it may be a good idea to introduce something like `//visibility:source` here, to make that mode of operation explicit in the .bp files.)",
